WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.143
<v Jordan Ruiz>Greg, thanks for joining — Priya's filled you in on the technical side, so let's talk numbers and terms.</v>

00:00:08.843 --> 00:00:24.271
<v Greg Hall>Appreciate it. I've got your proposal in front of me. The platform fee plus per-connector pricing makes sense, but at the volume we're asking for a 3-year commitment, I'd expect a meaningfully better rate than list.</v>

00:00:24.971 --> 00:00:34.829
<v Jordan Ruiz>That's fair, and a 3-year term is exactly the kind of commitment we like to reward. What number did you have in mind?</v>

00:00:35.529 --> 00:00:43.671
<v Greg Hall>We were hoping for 15% off list, with net-30 payment terms and no auto-escalation on renewal without our sign-off.</v>

00:00:44.371 --> 00:01:06.657
<v Jordan Ruiz>I can't commit to 15% on this call, but I don't think it's unreasonable for a 3-year deal — let me take it to my VP and come back with a real number rather than guess. Net-30 and renewal terms I can confirm now, those are standard for a deal this size.</v>

00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:15.929
<v Priya Nair>While Jordan checks on that — Greg, this is the point where we'd also want the security questionnaire sent over.</v>

00:01:16.629 --> 00:01:26.486
<v Greg Hall>Right, I'll send our standard vendor security questionnaire today. Given your October target, I'd like that turned around within a week if possible.</v>

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:37.471
<v Jordan Ruiz>We can do that — Devon already sent the SOC2 report, and our team turns questionnaires around fast, usually three to four business days.</v>

00:01:38.171 --> 00:01:46.743
<v Greg Hall>Good. One more thing — what does implementation support look like, and is that included or a separate line item?</v>

00:01:47.443 --> 00:02:03.729
<v Jordan Ruiz>Onboarding and the initial pipeline build-out are included in the platform fee for a deal this size. Ongoing premium support is a separate tier if you want faster SLAs, but standard support is included at no extra cost.</v>

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:16.000
<v Greg Hall>Okay, that's helpful. Get me a revised number on the discount and I can move quickly on our end — we want this live well before peak.</v>

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:25.700
<v Jordan Ruiz>Understood. I'll have an answer for you by early next week, and let's tentatively hold time the following week to finalize.</v>

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.971
<v Priya Nair>That works for us. Thanks, Jordan.</v>
